reaucracy and red tape frustrate the  American people gore stone and Poole  agree that the US should convert its air  traffic system from a government  bureaucracy to a self-supporting  nonprofit corporation  after all since commercialization  Canada's already safe skies have become  even safer the technology because of all  the real-time information available for  everyone means that if something does go  wrong you spot it more quickly and can  take corrective action so what happened  to Al Gore's attempt to modernize our  old-fashioned air traffic control system  it was a wonderful idea and it went  absolutely nowhere Congress just doesn't  like to give up control of anything  there's some things that the government  has to do there's some things the  government is very good at but air  traffic control is something the  government doesn't have to do and it's  not very good so the next time your  plane is delayed think about why you're  stuck maybe it's because of the weather  or maybe it's because of politics for  reason TV I'm Nick Gillespie
 

